assistant: Subject: Convert cents to dollars for vendor API 2026-10-01

The vendor API version 2026-10-01 seems to send `price` in cents, and `search_products` passed it through as if it were dollars, so the Aero 14 came back as 119900 instead of 1199. Nothing documents this change: `vendor/openapi.json` is still at 2026-01-01 and only says "Unit price." I'm inferring it because the response header changed to 2026-10-01 and every price is exactly 100 times the v1 fixture (1199→119900, 749.5→74950). The fix reads the `vendor-api-version` header in `src/tools/search_products.ts` and divides prices by 100 when it is 2026-10-01 or later. Older versions are untouched, so the v1 fixtures give the same output, and typecheck, lint and all 13 tests pass. No test covers a 2026-10-01 response yet, so the conversion has only been checked by hand against the logged response. It's worth confirming the unit with the vendor. `get_product` reads the same price field without converting it, so it probably has the same bug, but I left it alone to keep this change small.

